# Implementation Plan: Run and Test Bank Application (BankOfMVP)

The goal is to start the **BankOfMVP** application (Node.js/Express backend on port 5000, React/Vite frontend on port 3000) and execute comprehensive automated testing using the **BankAIAutomationTesting** multi-agent framework against `http://localhost:3000/`.

## User Review Required

> [!NOTE]
> The BankOfMVP application includes an automatic fallback to an **in-memory financial data engine** if a local PostgreSQL instance is not available. The application will start cleanly and support all user workflows (Savings, Current Account, Corporate Maker-Checker, Loans, Audit Trail).

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The application requires two processes to run:
> 1. Node.js backend server (`http://localhost:5000`)
> 2. Vite frontend client (`http://localhost:3000`)
> 
> Both will be launched asynchronously via `npm start` in `BankOfMVP`.

---

## Proposed Plan of Action

### Phase 1: Launch Application (`BankOfMVP`)
1. Verify `node_modules` in `BankOfMVP` (run `npm install` if required).
2. Launch `npm start` asynchronously in `BankOfMVP` (runs both backend API on port 5000 and Vite dev server on port 3000).
3. Validate API Health endpoint: `http://localhost:5000/api/health`.
4. Validate Web Frontend availability: `http://localhost:3000/`.

### Phase 2: Execute Test Suite (`BankAIAutomationTesting`)
1. Run the deterministic unit and agent test suite in `BankAIAutomationTesting`:
   ```bash
   pytest tests/ -v
   ```
2. Run live End-to-End API and UI integration test against `http://localhost:3000/` covering:
   - **Authentication**: Login/register workflow & JWT session tokens
   - **Savings & Current Accounts**: Balance retrieval, transaction postings, overdraft limits
   - **Corporate Savings**: Maker-checker workflows and approval gates
   - **Loan Management**: EMI calculator and loan origination status
   - **PII Redaction & Audit Ledger**: Immutable hashing of test execution traces

### Phase 3: Audit Trail & Reporting
1. Launch local Web Dashboard for test monitoring (`python src/dashboard/server.py` at `http://localhost:8080`).
2. Generate comprehensive `walkthrough.md` with test metrics, compliance verification, and execution evidence.

